          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "زرافة (zarāfa) is listed by Lane under z-r-f, with an explanation linking it to a word for \"a company\", because it seems an assemblage of animals; that looks like a folk explanation. EtymDB derives it from Syriac zarīpā; the origin is not certain. English giraffe comes from zarāfa through Italian."
            }
          ]
